<title>UK: Russia Novorossiisk port still shut, Tuapse closed.</title>
<headline>Russia Novorossiisk port still shut, Tuapse closed.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Black Sea oil terminal of Novorossiisk, Russia's main outlet to European markets, remained closed on Friday due to strong swells and high winds, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>The Black Sea port of Tuapse was also closed due to bad weather, the source added.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk shut at 0005 local time on Thursday morning after reopening briefly on Wednesday evening. The port had closed at midday on Monday due to bad weather.</p>
<p>The Sea Falcon II sailed from Novorossiisk on Thursday evening, the source added.</p>
<p>The other Black Sea port at Odessa and Latvia's port of Ventspils on the Baltic were operating normally.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7646</p>
